nancies.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"application_to_diagnosis\": [\n        \"The diagnostic criteria reinforce the strong likelihood of Dermatomyositis given the presence of poikiloderma and proximal muscle weakness, which are absent in Polymyositis.\",\n        \"The characterization of poikiloderma provides valuable differentiation from lupus-associated rashes, confirming that the observed skin findings are consistent with Dermatomyositis.\",\n        \"The emphasis on autoantibodies enriches diagnostic specificity and highlights the need for malignancy screening to rule out paraneoplastic involvement in this 66-year-old patient.\"\n    ],\n    \"selected_option\": \"Dermatomyositis\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.9,\n    \"self_questions\": [\n        \"Does the presence of poikiloderma and proximal weakness definitively exclude lupus?\",\n        \"Would autoantibody testing provide definitive diagnostic confirmation?\",\n        \"What tests are appropriate for malignancy screening in Dermatomyositis patients?\"\n    ],\n    \"needs_retrieval\": false\n}\n```",
