rs or immunomodulatory drugs that may precipitate GVHD, such as PD-1 inhibitors in this case. Studies have shown that plasma exchange effectively reduces debilitating GVHD symptoms in refractory cases.\",\n            \"Other immunosuppressive agents often used in refractory GVHD include tacrolimus, ruxolitinib, or mycophenolate mofetil. However, these may compromise the anti-tumor response, whereas plasma exchange avoids immunosuppression at the tumor level.\"\n        ]\n    },\n    \"impact_on_diagnosis\": [\n        \"The retrieved knowledge reaffirms that PD-1 inhibitors directly exacerbate GVHD risk post-HSCT due to enhanced T cell activation. This aligns with the patient’s timeline and presentation.\",\n        \"Differential knowledge confirms that the histopathological findings and presence of systemic multi-organ involvement support GVHD rather than an immune-related adverse event.\",\n        \"Details on plasma exchange highlight its role in depleting nivolumab (the presumed driver of GVHD), which aligns with the patient’s rapid improvement post-intervention.\"\n    ],\n    \"revised_selection\": \"Graft-versus-host disease\",\n    \"confidence_change\": \"Increased\"\n}\n```",
