ry markers.\"\n        ]\n    },\n    \"diagnostic_relevance\": [\n        {\n            \"topic\": \"Histology of bone marrow necrosis\",\n            \"relevance\": \"The histological features of BMN (e.g., necrotic debris, loss of hematopoietic architecture, and fibrin deposition) are consistent with the findings in the marrow specimen. Differentiating conditions like myelofibrosis and leukemia infiltration exhibit distinct histological patterns, which are not present in the provided image.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"topic\": \"Clinical features of acute monoblastic leukemia\",\n            \"relevance\": \"Acute monoblastic leukemia is a high-risk leukemia with common complications of DIC and TLS, both of which can cause ischemic damage to the bone marrow. The patient's persistent lower back pain and the histological findings strongly point toward BMN as the clinical outcome of these complications.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"diagnostic_confirmation\": \"The retrieved knowledge further supports bone marrow necrosis as the most likely diagnosis. The histopathological findings and clinical history align with BMN, specifically in the context of acute monoblastic leukemia with DIC and TLS.\"\n}\n```",
