h-dose dexamethasone testing can be used in some cases to differentiate ectopic ACTH syndrome from pituitary-dependent Cushing's disease, though its utility is limited by overlap between conditions. Inferior petrosal sinus sampling (IPSS) is the gold standard to confirm an ectopic source of ACTH by detecting a lack of ACTH gradient between central and peripheral blood samples. \\n2. Imaging: Cross-sectional imaging (CT/MRI) of the chest, abdomen, and pelvis should be conducted to locate the ectopic tumor. Functional imaging, such as 68Ga-DOTATATE PET-CT, is highly sensitive for detecting neuroendocrine neoplasms, which are often responsible for ectopic ACTH secretion.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"explanation\": [\n        \"The retrieved knowledge directly supports the diagnosis of ectopic ACTH secretion due to the confirmed presence of pancreatic adenocarcinoma and elevated ACTH and cortisol levels without suppression. The biochemical mechanism explains how high cortisol levels can cause unrelenting hypokalaemia through potassium wasting.\",\n        \"The rare association of pancreatic adenocarcinoma with ectopic ACTH production aligns with the confirmed biopsy findings of a poorly differentiated pancreatic mass in this case.\",\n        \"The diagnostic workup for ectopic Cushing's syndrome highlights the importance of biochemical tests (ACTH levels, cortisol dynamics) and imaging modalities. These approaches were already employed in this case, such as CT imaging revealing the pancreatic mass and the elevated ACTH and cortisol levels, which remain unsuppressed.\"\n    ]\n}\n```",
