sion due to increased erythropoiesis in β-thalassemia. It explains that while microfractures contribute to the structural weakening of bones, medullary expansion primarily causes ischemia directly leading to osteonecrosis. This aligns with the patient’s imaging findings and clinical history.\",\n    \"revised_selection\": \"Medullary expansion\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.95\n}\n```",
