cular or polymorphic as seen in disseminated VZV.\"\n        ]\n    },\n    \"relevance_to_case\": [\n        \"The imaging findings of multiple punctate microhemorrhages in the patient's corpus callosum and temporal lobes are highly specific for VZV encephalitis and distinguish it from HSV encephalitis or non-hemorrhagic encephalitis.\",\n        \"The patient's diffuse vesicular rash with hemorrhagic crusts, biopsy-proven VZV, and severe immunosuppression make disseminated VZV far more likely than systemic bacterial infection or HSV.\",\n        \"Systemic manifestations, including pneumonitis and encephalopathy, align with disseminated VZV and further differentiate it from bacterial sepsis.\"\n    ],\n    \"confidence_level\": 0.95,\n    \"needs_retrieval\": false\n}\n```",
